    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2741620/extras/5871dc79f5c5e226224a3e2be0be9259.avif?t=1725111836\" width=540 height=120 /></span><br><br><strong>GAME LENGTH: APPROX. 45 MINUTES</strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Charlotte is missing.</h2>A note has been left on her desk talking of &quot;the ancient evil&quot; and &quot;banishment to a different realm.&quot; The eldritch tome and an untranslated scrap she had been studying act as the only clues to her disappearance. Use clues found in the book to translate an ancient language, evade the lurking horrors, and solve the mystery of the strange objects around you!<br><br>This is a compact, detailed puzzle thriller similar to <u>The Room</u> and <u>Myst</u>. The player can inspect items, use clues, and slowly crack the mystery of the Great Library.<br><br>By John Szymanski, director of <u>My Friendly Neighborhood.</u><br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2741620/extras/a14c101c305bc89d3cb802a01f0efde1.avif?t=1725111836\" width=540 height=120 /></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Solve ancient puzzles, decode an eldritch language, and avoid the lurking horror all while sitting at a single desk<br></li><li>Tense and foreboding atmosphere where the stillness of the library can be shattered at any moment<br></li><li>High level of interactivity<br></li><li>Good for a single play session<br></li><li>Voiceover by Tom Schalk</li></ul><br>The original version was released in Dread X Collection 2.",
    "about_the_game": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2741620/extras/5871dc79f5c5e226224a3e2be0be9259.avif?t=1725111836\" width=540 height=120 /></span><br><br><strong>GAME LENGTH: APPROX. 45 MINUTES</strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Charlotte is missing.</h2>A note has been left on her desk talking of &quot;the ancient evil&quot; and &quot;banishment to a different realm.&quot; The eldritch tome and an untranslated scrap she had been studying act as the only clues to her disappearance. Use clues found in the book to translate an ancient language, evade the lurking horrors, and solve the mystery of the strange objects around you!<br><br>This is a compact, detailed puzzle thriller similar to <u>The Room</u> and <u>Myst</u>. The player can inspect items, use clues, and slowly crack the mystery of the Great Library.<br><br>By John Szymanski, director of <u>My Friendly Neighborhood.</u><br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2741620/extras/a14c101c305bc89d3cb802a01f0efde1.avif?t=1725111836\" width=540 height=120 /></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Solve ancient puzzles, decode an eldritch language, and avoid the lurking horror all while sitting at a single desk<br></li><li>Tense and foreboding atmosphere where the stillness of the library can be shattered at any moment<br></li><li>High level of interactivity<br></li><li>Good for a single play session<br></li><li>Voiceover by Tom Schalk</li></ul><br>The original version was released in Dread X Collection 2.",
